{"tool_name":"soda-solubility","contents":["oeb","bioschemas","biotools"],"fetched_metadata":{"biotools":{"id":"soda-solubility","home":"http://protein.bio.unipd.it/soda/","license":"CC-BY-NC-ND-4.0","summary":"Protein SOlubility based on Disorder and Aggregation","addition_date":"2018-03-12T09:31:50Z","last_update_date":"2024-11-25T14:23:38.672551Z","tool_type":["Web API","Web application"],"version":["1.0"],"biotools_curie":"biotools:soda-solubility","credit":[{"email":"silvio.tosatto@unipd.it","name":"Silvio C.E. Tosatto","orcidid":"http://orcid.org/0000-0003-4525-7793","typeEntity":"Person","typeRole":["Primary contact"],"url":"http://protein.bio.unipd.it"},{"name":"ELIXIR-ITA-PADOVA","url":"http://elixir.bio.unipd.it/"},{"name":"University of Padua, Department of Biomedical Sciences, BioComputing UP lab","url":"http://protein.bio.unipd.it/"}],"documentation":[{"type":["General"],"url":"http://protein.bio.unipd.it/soda/help"}],"edit_permission":{"type":"private"},"function":[{"input":[{"data":{"term":"Protein sequence","uri":"http://edamontology.org/data_2976"},"format":[{"term":"FASTA","uri":"http://edamontology.org/format_1929"}]}],"operation":[{"term":"Protein feature detection","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3092"},{"term":"Protein secondary structure prediction","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_0267"}],"output":[{"data":{"term":"Protein features","uri":"http://edamontology.org/data_1277"},"format":[{"term":"HTML","uri":"http://edamontology.org/format_2331"},{"term":"JSON","uri":"http://edamontology.org/format_3464"},{"term":"TSV","uri":"http://edamontology.org/format_3475"}]}]}],"maturity":"Mature","name":"SODA","operating_system":["Linux","Mac","Windows"],"owner":"ELIXIR-ITA-PADOVA","publication":[{"doi":"10.1093/nar/gkx412","metadata":{"abstract":"Solubility is an important, albeit not well understood, feature determining protein behavior. It is of paramount importance in protein engineering, where similar folded proteins may behave in very different ways in solution. Here we present SODA, a novel method to predict the changes of protein solubility based on several physico-chemical properties of the protein. SODA uses the propensity of the protein sequence to aggregate as well as intrinsic disorder, plus hydrophobicity and secondary structure preferences to estimate changes in solubility. It has been trained and benchmarked on two different datasets. The comparison to other recently published methods shows that SODA has state-of-the-art performance and is particularly well suited to predict mutations decreasing solubility. The method is fast, returning results for single mutations in seconds. A usage example estimating the full repertoire of mutations for a human germline antibody highlights several solubility hotspots on the surface.","authors":[{"name":"Paladin L."},{"name":"Piovesan D."},{"name":"Tosatto S.C.E."}],"citationCount":47,"date":"2017-07-03T00:00:00Z","journal":"Nucleic Acids Research","title":"SODA: Prediction of protein solubility from disorder and aggregation propensity"},"pmcid":"PMC7059794","pmid":"28505312","type":["Primary"]}],"topic":[{"term":"Protein disordered structure","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_3538"},{"term":"Protein sites, features and motifs","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_3510"},{"term":"Protein structure analysis","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_2814"}],"validated":1},"bioschemas":{"name":"SODA","home":"https://bio.tools/soda-solubility","license":"CC-BY-NC-ND-4.0","version":"1.0","summary":"Protein SOlubility based on Disorder and Aggregation","tool_type":"sc:SoftwareApplication"},"oeb":{"metrics":[{"@id":"https://openebench.bsc.es/monitor/metrics/biotools:soda-solubility:1.0/rest/protein.bio.unipd.it","@license":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/","@nmsp":"biotools","@type":"metrics","deprecated":true,"distribution":{"sourcecode":{"interpreted":true}},"project":{"build":{},"deployment":{},"documentation":{"general":true},"license":{"